      body: 'RoDTEP took effect on 1 January 2021 as the replacement for the Merchandise Exports from India Scheme (MEIS). In the WTO dispute India — Export Related Measures (DS541), brought by the United States, a panel report circulated on 31 October 2019 found MEIS to be a prohibited export subsidy, treating its duty-credit scrips as a direct transfer of funds rather than a remission of indirect taxes; India appealed in November 2019. RoDTEP was therefore built around refunding only those taxes that are actually embedded in exports and not refunded elsewhere.',
