      checkA: 'No. RoDTEP is framed as a remission of duties, taxes and levies already embedded in the exported product and not refunded under any other mechanism. That design is what separates it from MEIS, which the WTO panel treated as a prohibited export subsidy.',
      task: 'Revision task: note what this notification changed (only the end date, now 31 December 2026) and what it left unchanged (the rates and value caps in Appendix 4R and 4RE, and the eligible exporter categories).',
